anya: heads-up — my PR for the Throttling & Timeouts troubleshooting page failed snippet CI. The example that demonstrates 429 handling and timeout retries produced different console output than the recorded golden. PR: https://git.redwood/infr/docs/pull/478

frank: which example specifically? the backoff snippet?

anya: the JS SDK example that shows safe retries for idempotent requests. CI diff shows the example emitted `Stream truncated (client timeout)` instead of `Request failed: 429 Too Many Requests`. That makes the narrative confusing.

samir: runtime change note: we now sometimes return an intermittent EOF when the server-side connection is closed early for long-running tokens. It gets surfaced as a stream error in some client versions. We should clarify detection (status code vs stream error) in docs and show how to map both to the same retry decision.

lina: ok — proposed approach: show two minimal checks (status==429 || is_stream_eof(err)) and then call out Retry-After header when present. Also add a short blurb that non-idempotent mutations must not be retried automatically.

frank: agree. we should also replace the fixed backoff with an exponential backoff + full jitter snippet.

anya: sample I have now (failing) is inline in the PR. samir, can you paste the tiny canonical snippet we should show for the SDK? keep it simple for docs readers.

samir: posted minimal suggestion:

```
// pseudo-js
async function safeGenerate(client, req) {
  try {
    return await client.generate(req)
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 429 || isStreamTruncated(err)) {
      const wait = parseInt(err.headers?.['retry-after'] || '1', 10)
      await sleep(jitteredExponentialBackoff(wait))
      return await client.generate(req)
    }
    throw err
  }
}
```

lina: that's good. docs-bot: can we add a short note showing how to detect a stream truncation using the SDK's `StreamError` helper? Also suggest a one-line caution about not retrying `POST /v1/write`-style operations without idempotency keys.

docs-bot: snippet-lint: 1 mismatch (output tokenization differs) on the second run. Details: https://ci.redwood/infr/snippets/478

anya: thanks. frank, would you mind adding a micro-eval harness that simulates a flaky 429 endpoint so we can assert the sample behaves as expected? just 3 cases: immediate 429, stream EOF, and success.

frank: will do. I'll add a small YAML-based micro-eval and a note in the PR describing expected console output for each case. Also will update the prose to explain why the Retry-After header is preferred.

snippet-ci: automated check: withholding publish until docs PR merged and snippet outputs stabilized.

anya: perfect. once snippets pass CI, tag me and we'll land the runbook link to the error-ref entry for "429 / stream interruptions". Lina — can you review my wording about idempotency?

lina: yep, will review this afternoon. small nit: replace `sleep()` with `await timer()` helper in codeblock to match SDK samples.

frank: @snippet-ci please hold publishing until micro-eval added.

snippet-ci: acknowledged. queuing hold. :hourglass_flowing_sand:

anya: great teamwork 64f. I'll update the PR with samir's snippet and add a short FAQ note about why example outputs might differ across client versions.

lina: ping me when PR updated, will do a quick pass for clarity and the idempotency caution. :+1:
